// Wraps the three field-group pushes in one call, so newnode has a spare
// action left to name its return value (the new node's id) instead of
// returning the length expression directly.
//
// mk/ has no room for a sibling file, so this file was promoted into its
// own subdirectory to make room for the zero-argument fixtures/readers
// (fix1.id, m0.id) its cases and get/set/'s need to build and observe
// one full node in one call.

push_node(string kind, int a, int b, string s, string tstr, int[] l, int[] m) {
  push_kab(kind, a, b);
  push_st(s, tstr);
  push_lm(l, m);
} return void;
given boot_a ("num", 5, 0, "x", "ty", [1], [2]):() then k0_of:("num") then a0_of:(5) then s0_of:("x") then m0_of:([2])
given boot_a ("var", 9, 1, "y", "tz", [3], [4]):() then k0_of:("var") then a0_of:(9) then s0_of:("y") then m0_of:([4])
